# Public demo front door — automatic HTTPS for your domain.
#
# Caddy provisions and renews a real Let's Encrypt certificate for
# {$PUBLIC_DOMAIN} on its own, then reverse-proxies to the app. The app stays
# internal-only (no direct internet); only this proxy faces the public internet,
# exactly as in the sealed default — this just swaps the loopback:8000 front door
# for a public HTTPS one.
#
# Requirements: DNS for PUBLIC_DOMAIN points at this host, and ports 80 + 443 are
# open to the internet (Caddy needs 80 for the ACME challenge, 443 to serve).
{$PUBLIC_DOMAIN} {
	reverse_proxy app:8000
}
